{# velo_newsletter_compact content element — lighter, shorter alternative to velo_newsletter
   ("Draft 1 / Kompakter Inline-Banner" from a 3-way comparison, see the design-tokens repo).
   Single row on wider screens (icon · text · form), wraps to icon+text then form on mobile.
   Light --color-surface-2 background, no border/shadow -- reads as a quiet inline banner that
   sits in the page flow instead of a full dark attention-grabbing section like velo_newsletter.
   Red envelope icon makes the "this is about email" purpose obvious at a glance.

   Fully fixed trial element: no editable fields (see the DCA palette), headline/text/form are
   hardcoded right here instead of read from the model -- editors can only place or remove the
   whole element, not change its content. The headline field is left empty on the model (so the
   base template's own automatic headline_component never fires, see _base.html.twig's
   `{% if headline.text %}`) and this template owns the heading markup directly instead. #}
{% extends '@Contao/content_element/_base.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<section class="vw-newsletter-compact">
    <div class="vw-newsletter-compact__row">
        <div class="vw-newsletter-compact__icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <i data-lucide="mail" width="22" height="22"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="vw-newsletter-compact__text">
            <h2>Bleib auf dem Laufenden</h2>
            <p>Veloanlässe, Politisches und was sich in Wetzikon verändert — 10× im Jahr, direkt in dein Postfach.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vw-newsletter-compact__form">
            {{ insert_tag('insert_form::4')|raw }}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
